# Project Documentation

Before making any changes or extending this project, **always read the PRD.md file first**.

## Why PRD.md is Critical

The `PRD.md` file contains:
- Complete architecture overview of the ECS library
- Detailed documentation of all three games (Tetris, Vlak, Block Breaker)
- Build system and project structure
- Development guidelines and coding standards
- Extension points for adding new features

## When to Read PRD.md

**ALWAYS read PRD.md when:**
- Starting any new task in this project
- Adding new games or examples
- Modifying the ECS library
- Extending existing games
- Debugging issues
- Understanding how components work
- Learning about the message system
- Understanding the factory pattern used in games

## Quick Reference

After reading PRD.md, you'll understand:
- How the ECS (Entity-Component-System) pattern works
- The lifecycle of components and game objects
- The message-driven architecture
- How to use Builder pattern for creating entities
- How each game implements its specific mechanics
- The common patterns used across all games

**Read PRD.md first, then proceed with your task.**
